# Performance

Measure before optimizing and protect constrained devices by default.

- Stream the raw source; never load the complete local dataset into memory.
- Return bounded, version-aware cursor pages and aggregates, with Finding
  Detail loaded only on demand.
- Run filtering, sorting, search suggestions, faceting, aggregation,
  pagination, and export in ClickHouse behind bounded, parameterized GraphQL
  queries (`first` clamped, keyset cursors) and the server-side export job,
  never on the React render thread and never over a full client-side copy.
- Keep SSE `DatasetEvent`s small and versioned: notifications and single-row
  upserts, coalesced into `findings-changed` under load; stream ClickHouse
  output (`JSONCompactEachRow`, `CSVWithNames`) instead of buffering in Node.
- Bound concurrency, memory, response sizes, and export work.
- Avoid request waterfalls and duplicate export downloads. Let Apollo Client
  own GraphQL cache and request lifecycle.
- Diagnose build or runtime regressions from observed evidence, fix
  incrementally, and rerun only the focused check needed for the changed area.
